{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unhygenic-reversible-mare","creation_channel":"cli","description":"The completion-verifier close precheck (_check_work_landed -> _referencing_commits -> commit_impact.referencing_commits) walks all code history and resolves every commit's rebar-ticket: trailer via resolve_ticket_id. When trailers are aliases, the resolver ran a fresh full-store alias scan (os.listdir(tracker) + per-ticket CREATE/SNAPSHOT JSON read) per distinct alias -- O(distinct_aliases x store). On the production-scale store (5300+ ticket dirs) a single close hung 70+ minutes at high CPU.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- referencing_commits builds an alias index once (single store pass) and threads it into resolve_ticket_id, so the number of full tracker-root scans does not grow with the number of distinct alias trailers in history.\n- Correctness unchanged: same commits credited to the same tickets (full/short/alias/Jira/prefix forms all still resolve identically).\n- A perf-contract unit test asserts bounded store scans for many distinct alias trailers, RED before the fix.\n- No behavior change to resolve_ticket_id's single-id callers (alias_index is optional).\n\nFix: add _ids.build_alias_index + _effective_alias_for_dir (extracted from _scan_alias), optional alias_index param on resolve_ticket_id, build+thread the index in commit_impact.referencing_commits, re-export build_alias_index from _engine_support.resolver.","id":"4234-821b-150c-461b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"referencing_commits alias resolution is O(distinct_aliases x store)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787516971492831001,"uuid":"b86f8804-6d17-43f6-b9b2-3f3c617e6358"}